# A spell with {X} cast for its flashback cost still announces X and pays it (Snapcaster Mage's ruling; CR 107.3a), and on
# the stack X is the number announced (CR 202.3e). Bot1 casts Fireball (X = 1) at Bot2, then Snapcaster Mage gives it
# flashback for its mana cost, {X}{R}; cast again with X = 1 it is mana value 2, so Bot2's Spell Snare ("counter target
# spell with mana value 2") counters it, and it is exiled rather than put into the graveyard (CR 702.34a). Bot2 took 1.

